# cp.async.bulk.tensor (PTX ISA §9.7.9.26.5.2): a shared side, its
# address traced, and a global side, whose address the tensor map
# holds; the bytes of both are the tensor map's, so they are unknown in
# every total, each copy reads `bytes ? (not counted)`, the instruction
# table counts each form as a copy of unknown bytes, the kernel's
# unknowns list them, and a loop holding one
# has no global bytes per CTA. Each guarded form runs once per CTA, on
# the thread its guard selects, %tid.x == 0.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --annotate %fixtures/micro/tensor_copies.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/tensor_copies.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
ANN: {{^}}.visible .entry micro_tensor_copy_forms( // block 128×1×1 | shared memory 16,392 B/CTA | per CTA: global load ? B, store ? B; shared load ? B, store ? B; shared::cluster store ? B{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	cp.async.bulk.tensor.1d.shared::cta.global.mbarrier::complete_tx::bytes.tile [%r3], [%rd1, {%r2}], [%r4]; // bytes ? (not counted) | shared store [smem] | global load addr ? (the tensor map holds the address){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	@%p1 cp.async.bulk.tensor.2d.shared::cta.global.mbarrier::complete_tx::bytes [%r3+1024], [%rd1, {%r2, %r1}], [%r4]; // warp 0 × lane 0 | exec 1/CTA | bytes ? (not counted) | shared store [smem + 1024] | global load addr ? (the tensor map holds the address){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	@%p1 cp.async.bulk.tensor.2d.tile::gather4.shared::cta.global.mbarrier::complete_tx::bytes [%r3], [%rd1, {%r2, %r1, %r1, %r1, %r1}], [%r4]; // warp 0 × lane 0 | exec 1/CTA | bytes ? (not counted) | shared store [smem] | global load addr ? (the tensor map holds the address){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	@%p1 cp.async.bulk.tensor.2d.shared::cluster.global.mbarrier::complete_tx::bytes.multicast::cluster [%r3], [%rd1, {%r2, %r1}], [%r4], %rs1; // warp 0 × lane 0 | exec 1/CTA | bytes ? (not counted) | shared::cluster store [smem] | global load addr ? (the tensor map holds the address){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	@%p1 cp.async.bulk.tensor.1d.global.shared::cta.bulk_group [%rd1, {%r2}], [%r3]; // warp 0 × lane 0 | exec 1/CTA | bytes ? (not counted) | global store addr ? (the tensor map holds the address) | shared load [smem]{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	@%p1 cp.async.bulk.tensor.2d.global.shared::cta.tile::scatter4.bulk_group.L2::cache_hint [%rd1, {%r2, %r1, %r1, %r1, %r1}], [%r3], %rd3; // warp 0 × lane 0 | exec 1/CTA | bytes ? (not counted) | global store addr ? (the tensor map holds the address) | shared load [smem]{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}$L__BB3_1: // loop: trips 4 | warp * × lane * | exec 512/CTA{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd4], %r1; // global store [4·%tid.x + 512·iv[$L__BB3_1] + param_0] sectors/req 4–5 (ideal 4){{$}}
CHECK-LABEL: kernel micro_tensor_copy_forms
CHECK: cp.async.bulk.tensor.2d.shared::cta.global.mbarrier::complete_tx::bytes{{ +}}shared store on 1 thread in 1 warp (%tid.x == 0){{ +}}[smem + 1024]
CHECK-NEXT: cp.async.bulk.tensor.2d.shared::cta.global.mbarrier::complete_tx::bytes{{ +}}global load on 1 thread in 1 warp (%tid.x == 0){{ +}}unknown: the tensor map holds the address
CHECK: cp.async.bulk.tensor.2d.shared::cluster.global.mbarrier::complete_tx::bytes.multicast::cluster{{ +}}shared::cluster store on 1 thread in 1 warp (%tid.x == 0){{ +}}[smem]
CHECK-NEXT: cp.async.bulk.tensor.2d.shared::cluster.global.mbarrier::complete_tx::bytes.multicast::cluster{{ +}}global load on 1 thread in 1 warp (%tid.x == 0){{ +}}unknown: the tensor map holds the address
CHECK: cp.async.bulk.tensor.1d.global.shared::cta.bulk_group{{ +}}global store on 1 thread in 1 warp (%tid.x == 0){{ +}}unknown: the tensor map holds the address
CHECK-NEXT: cp.async.bulk.tensor.1d.global.shared::cta.bulk_group{{ +}}shared load on 1 thread in 1 warp (%tid.x == 0){{ +}}[smem]
CHECK: global -> shared copy ? B{{ +}}6
CHECK: shared -> global copy ? B{{ +}}3
CHECK: global -> shared::cluster copy ? B{{ +}}2
CHECK: unknowns:
CHECK-NEXT: global load with statically unknown byte count x8
CHECK-NEXT: global store with statically unknown byte count x3
CHECK-NEXT: shared load with statically unknown byte count x3
CHECK-NEXT: shared store with statically unknown byte count x6
CHECK-NEXT: shared::cluster store with statically unknown byte count x2
CHECK-LABEL: kernel micro_tensor_copy_in_loop
